  "version": "as-filed",
  "operative_text": "(a_in_person_id)\n(section) Sec. 240A(1)(a)\n(quote) Except as provided in subsection (2), a qualified elector who votes in a primary or general election, either in person at the polls or in person in the office of the circuit clerk, shall present a government issued photo identification before being allowed to vote.\n(section) Sec. 240A(2)(a)\n(quote) An elector living and voting in a state-licensed care facility shall not be required to show a government-issued photo identification before being allowed to vote.\n(b_no_id_remedy)\n(section) Sec. 240A(1)(b)\n(quote) A qualified elector who does not have a government issued photo identification and who cannot afford such identification may obtain a state-issued photo identification free of charge from the Mississippi Department of Public Safety.\n(section) Sec. 240A(2)(c)\n(quote) An elector who has a government-issued photo identification, but is unable to present that identification when voting, shall file a provisional ballot, and the elector, within five (5) days after the election, shall present the government issued photo identification to the appropriate circuit clerk.\n(c_mail_ballot_id) not stated.\n(d_proof_of_citizenship) not stated.\n(e_other_rule)\n(section) Sec. 240A(3)\n(quote) This provision shall not be construed to require photo identification to register to vote.\n(section) Ballot explanation\n(quote) This proposed constitutional amendment will require qualified electors to present a government-issued photo identification before being allowed to vote.\n(other) Concurrent resolution proposing new Section 240A of the Mississippi Constitution; ballot explanation text",
